  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message criticizing media credibility",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'the people don't believe our bullshit anymore', which serves as the core message of the meme. The user identifies with the sentiment expressed — the disillusionment of the public toward mainstream media narratives — and sees themselves as part of that collective skepticism. The projection is implicit, not deictic (e.g., no 'you' or 'me'), but the tone and content of the text create a direct psychological alignment with the viewer's own perception of media distrust.",
